diagram: Prioritize prevention via short leash | Protect handlers from panic bites | Seek prompt veterinary evaluation
visual: Conceptual emergency readiness sequence emphasizing short-leash prevention, bite protection for panicked pets, and urgent vet transport.
action: Treat short-leash prevention on open multi-use lands as the primary lifesaving measure because high-force devices act faster than unprepared owners can respond. @L10
action: Recognize that even gentle dogs in sudden pain or panic frequently bite owners during stressful incidents; protect hands/face, stay calm, and call for immediate assistance if an incident occurs. @L10,M06
action: Seek immediate veterinary evaluation for any pet that suffers even a brief restraining or cable encounter because internal bruising, tendon damage, swelling, or airway injury can worsen after release. @L10
failure: Assuming a limping dog is fine after a brief mechanical pinch overlooks hidden crush trauma, ischemia, or soft-tissue infection. @L10
verify: Emergency vet contact info is stored offline before rural outings, and short-leash prevention stays enforced. @L10
stop: Stop and seek emergency veterinary care immediately after any pet encounter with a mechanical capture device, wire, or distressed wildlife. @L10
reviewer: Veterinarian and pet-safety reviewer

Z07-P19 | Non-Tampering Laws and Safe Distance Around Lawful Equipment | New manuscript (Z07 P18 legal and safety)
objective: Prevent both personal injury and criminal trap-interference violations when encountering lawfully placed seasonal gear.
applies: Encountering tagged seasonal equipment on open public lands where trapping is lawful.
equipment: None—observe from distance and move on.
diagram: Respect non-interference statutes | Keep hands and boots completely clear | Detour smoothly on main trail
visual: Conceptual correct-versus-incorrect comparison contrasting lawful hands-off detouring against illegal tampering or springing.
action: Understand that Minnesota law prohibits intentionally tampering with, springing, damaging, or stealing lawfully placed traps or snares. @L01,L09
action: Avoid approaching or touching suspected equipment both to comply with statute and to prevent severe crush injuries from stored spring energy. @L09,L11
